control_cli_events {"model": "gpt-6-luna", "events": "{\"type\":\"thread.started\",\"thread_id\":\"01a1679d-bdd9-74d0-94c7-1b6c81ec4c6d\"}\n{\"type\":\"turn.started\"}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_0\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"{\\\"task_summary\\\":\\\"Implement `invert` in `solution.py` and add standard-library `unittest` coverage in `test_solution.py` for ordinary, boundary, and empty inputs, preserving insertion order of keys grouped by value. Verify with unittest discovery.\\\",\\\"constraints\\\":[\\\"Work only in the supplied task workspace; do not access parent repositories or external services.\\\",\\\"Use Python 3.11+ and the standard library.\\\",\\\"Do not mutate input collections.\\\",\\\"Maintain type hints.\\\",\\\"No algorithmic complexity constraint is imposed.\\\",\\\"`test_solution.py` must contain at least two passing unittest test methods exercising the public API.\\\"],\\\"success_criteria\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SC-1\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"The requested implementation file exists.\\\",\\\"check\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"file_exists\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"solution.py\\\"}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SC-2\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"The implementation file compiles.\\\",\\\"check\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"command\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"python -m py_compile solution.py\\\",\\\"expected\\\":{\\\"exit_code\\\":0}}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SC-3\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"The `invert` function is defined in `solution.py` with a return annotation.\\\",\\\"check\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"regex\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"solution.py\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"def\\\\\\\\s+invert\\\\\\\\s*\\\\\\\\([^)]*\\\\\\\\)\\\\\\\\s*->\\\"}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SC-4\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"The public tests define at least two unittest test methods.\\\",\\\"check\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"regex\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"test_solution.py\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"(?s)(?:class\\\\\\\\s+\\\\\\\\w+\\\\\\\\s*\\\\\\\\([^)]*unittest\\\\\\\\.TestCase[^)]*\\\\\\\\)\\\\\\\\s*:[^\\\\\\\\n]*(?:\\\\\\\\n|$).*?def\\\\\\\\s+test_\\\\\\\\w+\\\\\\\\s*\\\\\\\\(self[^)]*\\\\\\\\)\\\\\\\\s*:.*?def\\\\\\\\s+test_\\\\\\\\w+\\\\\\\\s*\\\\\\\\(self[^)]*\\\\\\\\)\\\\\\\\s*:|def\\\\\\\\s+test_\\\\\\\\w+\\\\\\\\s*\\\\\\\\(self[^)]*\\\\\\\\)\\\\\\\\s*:.*?def\\\\\\\\s+test_\\\\\\\\w+\\\\\\\\s*\\\\\\\\(self[^)]*\\\\\\\\)\\\\\\\\s*:)\\\"}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SC-5\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"The test module compiles.\\\",\\\"check\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"command\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"python -m py_compile test_solution.py\\\",\\\"expected\\\":{\\\"exit_code\\\":0}}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SC-6\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"The tests exercise public behavior for ordinary, boundary, and empty inputs, check the grouped key ordering, and verify that input is not mutated.\\\",\\\"check\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"llm_judge\\\",\\\"rubric\\\":\\\"Read `test_solution.py` and assess whether its unittest methods exercise the public `invert` API for ordinary, boundary, and empty inputs; verify the expected grouping of keys by value in dictionary insertion order; and include a check that the input is unchanged after calling the API. Judge only content visible in the file.\\\"}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SC-7\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"The implementation groups input keys by their values in insertion order, returns `{}` for empty input, and does not mutate the input.\\\",\\\"check\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"llm_judge\\\",\\\"rubric\\\":\\\"Read `solution.py` and assess whether the `invert` implementation groups keys under their corresponding values, preserves each group's key order according to input dictionary insertion order, returns an empty dictionary for empty input, and avoids mutating the input collection. Also assess whether the implementation uses type hints. Judge only content visible in the file.\\\"}}],\\\"verification\\\":[{\\\"command\\\":\\\"python -m py_compile solution.py\\\",\\\"expected\\\":{\\\"exit_code\\\":0}},{\\\"command\\\":\\\"python -m py_compile test_solution.py\\\",\\\"expected\\\":{\\\"exit_code\\\":0}},{\\\"command\\\":\\\"python -m unittest discover -v\\\",\\\"expected\\\":{\\\"exit_code\\\":0}}],\\\"stop_conditions\\\":[],\\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"The named files are relative to the supplied task workspace; `solution.py` and `test_solution.py` may not exist yet and may be created.\\\",\\\"The requested \u201cboundary\u201d inputs are interpreted as edge cases appropriate to a mapping accepted by `invert`; no specific boundary values were supplied.\\\",\\\"The public API is a callable named `invert` defined in `solution.py`; its exact parameter and return types are not specified, so suitable type annotations must be chosen during implementation.\\\",\\\"The request specifies ordinary, boundary, and empty-input tests; the parenthetical invalid-numeric case is treated as an alternative only if no collection input is accepted, while the stated grouping behavior implies collection input.\\\",\\\"The supplied unittest discovery command is run from the task workspace, and the test module is discoverable by default unittest discovery.\\\"]}\"}}\n{\"type\":\"turn.completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":17389,\"cached_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":925,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":0}}\n"}
